<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Sign in with Apple, which App Store Review Guideline 4.8 obliges.
	     This app offers Google SSO, and 4.8 requires an equivalent
	     privacy-preserving login option beside any third-party or social
	     login; Sign in with Apple is the cheapest way to satisfy it. Shipping
	     Google alone is not a choice that is available
	     (design/FIREBASE.md, the amended §9.2 decision).

	     CORRECTED 2026-09-21. This comment used to read "Ali's son has an
	     Apple account and no Google one, so this is not a nice-to-have:
	     without it he cannot join a shared set list at all." That is
	     backwards. Apple does not offer Sign in with Apple to an account
	     under the age threshold, so it is Google sign-in that works for him
	     and Apple's that does not. The entitlement stays regardless: 4.8,
	     not any one user, is what requires it.

	     The matching capability (APPLE_ID_AUTH, with PRIMARY_APP_CONSENT) is
	     enabled on the App ID com.irllabs.scoranger; this entitlement
	     without that capability fails code signing, and that capability
	     without this entitlement is what made the button do nothing in
	     build 183. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Universal links, which is what makes the invitation TAPPABLE.
	     Without this key the entitlement is absent from the signed app and
	     iOS never consults the association: tapping
	     https://scoranger.web.app/invite/[id] opens Safari and the invitee
	     lands on a web page instead of the join screen. The AASA has been
	     live and correct at that host the whole time (HTTPS, 200,
	     application/json, no redirect, appIDs
	     V9DBGV72NL.com.irllabs.scoranger, components /invite/*), so this one
	     missing key was the whole gap.

	     The matching capability (ASSOCIATED_DOMAINS) is enabled on the App
	     ID and the ACTIVE App Store profile carries
	     com.apple.developer.associated-domains = *, so this signs without
	     touching the profile. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:scoranger.web.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
